-- ===========================================================================
-- Paragon: server-side content that had no SQL file of its own.
--
-- Both blocks below existed only as live state on the origin box -- the spells
-- were applied by hand from a code block in the documentation, and the title
-- was baked straight into that box's CharTitles.dbc inside its docker image.
-- Neither was ever emitted by Tools/paragon_client_patch.py, so a fresh host
-- applying only 01_paragon_content.sql gets neither, with no error and no log
-- line.
--
-- Apply to: acore_world       (after 01_paragon_content.sql)
-- Then:     RESTART THE WORLDSERVER -- the *_dbc override tables are merged
--           into the DBC stores only at startup.
-- Safe to re-run: every statement is DELETE + INSERT on an explicit id.
-- ===========================================================================


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 1. The three reward-track aura spells.
--
-- Referenced from paragon_rework_track.lua:2151-2153 as OOC_MOVE_SPEED,
-- SWIM_SPEED and QUICK_MOUNT (milestones 50, 150 and 100).
--
-- !! 1900005 ALSO GATES A COMPILED-IN CORE PATCH !!
-- Unit.cpp:11781 reads `if (HasAura(1900005))` to apply the mount-cast-time
-- reduction. Without this row that branch can never be taken, so the host
-- rebuilds the core for a feature that cannot fire.
--
-- Rows dumped from the live acore_world.spell_dbc, not retyped from the docs,
-- so every column matches what is actually running.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DELETE FROM `spell_dbc` WHERE `ID` IN (1900003, 1900004, 1900005);
